    "result_text": "The full test suite passes (`BUILD SUCCESS`). There's only one test class (`AcceptanceTest`; the other two files are support classes), and it's green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the tenure-based membership rule in `OwnerMapper.membershipLevel(...)` (`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/mapper/OwnerMapper.java`):\n\n- **Raised the cap** `MAX_MEMBERSHIP_LEVEL` from 3 to 4, since level 4 is now attainable.\n- **Added `TENURE_LEVEL_DAYS = 365`** \u2014 an owner must be registered for *strictly more than* 365 days to qualify for level 4.\n- **Added a `tenureDays(owner)` helper** computing whole days from `registrationDate` to `LocalDate.now()` (returning 0 when there's no registration date), and awarded the 4th level only when `tenureDays(owner) > 365`.\n- Added the `java.time.temporal.ChronoUnit` import.\n\nBecause a newly created owner's `registrationDate` defaults to today, its tenure is 0, so it never clears the threshold. A new owner with an email (+1) and `namesakeCount == 0` (+1) lands at level 3 \u2014 exactly what the `coreNewOwnerCappedAtLevel3` acceptance test asserts (`membershipLevel == 3`), and the household size plays no part in the level, consistent with the spec.",
